<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Syros</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Syros is a Greek island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyclades">Cyclades</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean Sea</a>. Its town, Ermoupoli, founded by refugees from Chios and Psara during the War of Independence, was the leading port and commercial centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> in the mid-nineteenth century, with shipyards and textile mills. It is the administrative capital of the Cyclades, and the island has a long-established Catholic community.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/syros.jpg" alt="Syros" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Peter Schaefer, http://www.reserv-a-rt.de · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Syros_Ano_Syros_u_Ermoupolis140707.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
